node_modules/
dist/
dist-bridge/
**/target/

# Gradle's output for the two Android plugins, and the copy of wry's kotlin that Tauri drops beside
# it. Both are regenerated by every build; committing them put 650-odd files in the first `git add`.
**/android/build/
**/android/.tauri/
**/android/.gradle/
.gradle/
**/src-tauri/generated/

# The generated Android and iOS projects — except that `gen/android` is not entirely generated, and
# the parts that are not would be lost on a clean checkout without the exceptions below. Each of
# them is hand-written and load-bearing:
#
#   MainActivity.kt        Shiver's back-button handling and the window-inset padding that keeps the
#                          page clear of the system bars (§7 of HANDOVER — css cannot do it)
#   AndroidManifest.xml    allowBackup off, and the network security config
#   res/xml/               those rules themselves; src/debug/res/xml relaxes cleartext for the dev
#                          server, and only for debug builds
#   app/build.gradle.kts   the release signing config, compileSdk 36, the cleartext placeholders
#                          and the extra dependencies
#
# Losing any of it is a silent regression: the app still builds, just without the behaviour. Written
# as `gen/**` rather than `gen/` on purpose — git does not look inside an excluded *directory*, so
# every directory on the way down to a kept file has to be re-included too, which is why this list
# is longer than the four files it protects. Re-check them after any `tauri android init`.
**/src-tauri/gen/**

!**/src-tauri/gen/android/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/build.gradle.kts
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/com/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/com/shiver/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/com/shiver/mobile/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/com/shiver/mobile/MainActivity.kt
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/res/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/res/xml/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/res/xml/*.xml
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/debug/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/debug/res/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/debug/res/xml/
!**/src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/debug/res/xml/*.xml
*.log

# editor backups. `icon.png~` — a 134KB copy of the old icon — was committed by a `git add -A` and
# had to be taken out again; it is cheaper to never take one in.
*~
*.bak
*.orig
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local

# a read-only checkout of Sharkord, kept for reference while building against its client
reference/

# built android artifacts, handed over for testing rather than committed
*.apk

# Android release signing — never commit
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Our own notes, which are ours: CHANGELOG.md is a running record of what was asked for and why,
# Shiver.md is the design, security model and operational detail, DESIGN.md the original spec. None
# of it is anyone else's business, and the changelog in particular reads as a conversation.
#
# Written as a blanket ignore with exceptions rather than a list, so a note added later is private
# by default rather than private only if someone remembers to add it here.
*.md

# The two that are genuinely for other people: the front page of the repo, and the instructions a
# server admin reads when installing the companion plugin (which also ships inside its zip).
!README.md
!plugin/README.md
